From 832a2b852e6abc2ad8120c505b5499d31c606106 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 12:12:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 40/75] wm: split an in-activity alert dialog into its own
 modal window (ARC)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A TYPE_APPLICATION dialog window with FLAG_DIM_BEHIND (an AlertDialog) added on
top of a non-dialog activity — e.g. the "won't be allowed" alert over the
full-screen PermissionController page — shares the activity's task. Its layer
inherits the host TaskId, so the ARC compositor unions its centered bounds into
the host footprint and grows the host window.

Classify such a dialog window and stamp METADATA_IS_FLOATING_ACTIVITY on its own
surface (WindowState.setInitialSurfaceControlProperties). The compositor strips
its TaskId and routes the subtree to its own centered modal window
(SurfaceFlinger Layer::addChild / WaylandHwc2Composer), leaving the host at its
natural size. Gated to opaque host tasks (!task.isTranslucent) so a translucent
dialog task (e.g. PackageInstaller's concentric windows) is not fragmented per
window — that case is composited as one centered modal via IsDialogTask.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: If28308f77fecebff7e719d22f9c8ce097076b1cf
---
 .../com/android/server/wm/WindowState.java    | 33 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowState.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowState.java
index 24619ca6a874..ff5112ee0bce 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowState.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowState.java
@@ -5960,6 +5960,39 @@ class WindowState extends WindowContainer<WindowState> implements WindowManagerP
         mViewVisibility = viewVisibility;
     }
 
+    /**
+     * An AlertDialog-style window: a TYPE_APPLICATION window (i.e. NOT the
+     * activity's TYPE_BASE_APPLICATION main window) that dims behind itself,
+     * shown on top of an opaque (non-translucent) host task — e.g. the
+     * "won't be allowed" alert over the full-screen PermissionController page.
+     * Such a dialog window otherwise inherits the host TaskId and the compositor
+     * unions its centered bounds into the host footprint, auto-expanding the
+     * host window. We classify it as a dialog and split it into its own centered
+     * modal: reuse METADATA_IS_FLOATING_ACTIVITY, which the compositor strips the
+     * TaskId from and routes to a standalone modal window (SurfaceFlinger
+     * Layer::addChild / WaylandHwc2Composer).
+     *
+     * Excludes translucent dialog *tasks* (e.g. PackageInstaller's concentric
+     * windows) — those are composited as ONE centered modal via IsDialogTask and
+     * must not be fragmented into a modal per window.
+     */
+    private boolean isFloatingDialogWindow() {
+        if (mAttrs.type != TYPE_APPLICATION
+                || (mAttrs.flags & FLAG_DIM_BEHIND) == 0) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        final Task task = getTask();
+        return task != null && !task.isTranslucent(null /* starting */);
+    }
+
+    @Override
+    void setInitialSurfaceControlProperties(SurfaceControl.Builder b) {
+        if (isFloatingDialogWindow()) {
+            b.setMetadata(SurfaceControl.METADATA_IS_FLOATING_ACTIVITY, 1);
+        }
+        super.setInitialSurfaceControlProperties(b);
+    }
+
     SurfaceControl getClientViewRootSurface() {
         return mWinAnimator.getSurfaceControl();
     }
